{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The fee can only stand if the driver held position inside the pickup geofence for a continuous dwell of at least the free waiting period in force, and trip_record.platform_policy fixes that period at 300 seconds for this trip (free_wait_sec 300, arrival_marker BUTTON). POL-NS-01(c) measures that dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 2026-08-06T12:30:00+08:00, not from the 12:29:55 arrival tap, so the clock the driver's own account relies on is the wrong clock.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00211", "EV-GPS-00211"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.thresholds.minimum_dwell_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On the fixes this trace does record, the driver's longest continuous in-geofence run is 220 seconds (12:30:00 to 12:33:40, 23 fixes) against the 300-second minimum - a shortfall of 80 seconds - so POL-NS-01(c) is not satisfied and POL-NS-06 makes the cancellation fee non-chargeable. EV-GPS-00211 is impaired at weight 0.39 on issues GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW and LOW_COVERAGE, and this reading is taken from the fixes it does record rather than from anything the trace fails to show.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00211", "EV-TRIP-00211"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.longest_run_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.39
    },
    {
      "text": "The second in-geofence run, 112 seconds from 12:36:28 to 12:38:20, cannot be added to the first. POL-NS-06(i) permits separate in-geofence intervals to be summed only where a traffic_advisory covering the pickup road is present and populated, and EV-ADVIS-00211-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0 - an absence that is itself citable - so the derived limb records the summation route as unavailable on both advisory_missing and excursion_unmeasurable grounds, and 220 seconds is the effective dwell.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00211-01", "EV-GPS-00211"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.limb.available",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The 500-second figure in derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run is a first-fix-to-last-fix envelope that spans the 168-second gap; it is not a continuous dwell. POL-NS-01(c) requires continuity, and the only route to treating separated intervals as one continuous presence is POL-NS-06(i), which the MISSING advisory closes, so the envelope cannot stand in for the 300 seconds the clause demands. EV-GPS-00211 is impaired at 0.39 on GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW and LOW_COVERAGE.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00211"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.39
    },
    {
      "text": "The 168-second outage from 12:33:40 to 12:36:28 falls inside the waiting window and exceeds the 120-second limb of POL-NS-08(b), so as a matter of policy the trace does not establish that the driver held the kerb across it. That stretch cannot be credited to him as dwell, and it cannot convert a 220-second run into the 300-second continuous dwell POL-NS-01(c) requires. EV-GPS-00211 is impaired at 0.39 on GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW and LOW_COVERAGE, coverage being 84.3 per cent against the 90 per cent threshold.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00211"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-NS-01"]
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-12 cannot be used to fill that gap with platform telemetry: it applies only where arrival_marker is GPS_AUTO with the platform's own arrival, wait_timer_started and wait_timer_expired events stating the geofence test. This trip's arrival_marker is BUTTON with a driver-pressed arrival at 12:29:55, so the waiting period is not established as served by any carrier independent of the exported trace, and POL-NS-01 limbs (b) and (c) stand on the trace alone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00211", "EV-GPS-00211"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-12", "POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The remedy follows from POL-NS-06: the 4.00 SGD cancellation fee is not chargeable and is refunded to the rider in full, and because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full POL-NS-07 gives the driver no compensation at all. The sum to be returned is the cancellation-fee line on a fare whose payment_status is CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and the rider is the filing party, so under POL-GEN-03 the whole contested 4.00 is hers. The refund does not depend on her own movements, POL-NS-06 refunding whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she answered messages.",
