{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.75,
    "explanation": "To both parties. The driver pressed 'arrived' at 12:29:55 and cancelled at 12:38:20 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW (EV-TRIP-00211). POL-NS-01(a) is met, and the marker was not false under POL-NS-05: the trace places the driver 18.1 to 29.3 m from the pin and stationary, nowhere near the 300 m distance trigger or the 15 km/h speed trigger, so the waiting clock is not recomputed. POL-NS-01(d) is also met (no boarding event, driver-terminated under RIDER_NO_SHOW).\n\nThe case turns on limb (c). It requires a continuous in-geofence dwell of at least 300 s (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec), measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 12:30:00. The GPS trace EV-GPS-00211 is IMPAIRED at weight 0.39 on issue codes GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW and LOW_COVERAGE. It records in-geofence fixes from 12:30:00 to 12:33:40 (220 s) and from 12:36:28 to 12:38:20 (112 s), with a 168 s gap in between (12:33:40 to 12:36:28) that exceeds the 120 s limb of POL-NS-08(b) and sits inside the waiting window. Over that stretch the trace cannot read. The limb is therefore UNDECIDED over it: the rider's figure of 220 s with an 80 s shortfall is not established (the gap is a recording outage, not a fix showing the driver drove away), and the driver's figure of 500 s is not established either (that value is a first-fix-to-last-fix envelope spanning the gap, not a continuous run). The rider's POL-NS-06(i) summation point is moot because the driver does not rely on summing separate intervals.\n\nThe chat log EV-CHAT-00211 is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 and carries the driver's message of 12:35:10 from inside the gap, between the in-geofence readings this test admits. That contemporaneous record from inside the unobserved stretch counts under POL-GEN-02(2): the confidence cap is the MAXIMUM of the two weights (1.0), not the minimum (0.39), and the impaired trace is not the only evidence, so POL-NS-08's PARTIAL_REFUND ceiling and POL-NS-09(e) are not engaged.\n\nBecause limb (c) is undecided, neither a payment that needs it to hold (POL-NS-07) nor a full refund that needs it to fail (POL-NS-06) is supported. Under POL-NS-08 the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee (EV-FARE-00211; payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) is split rather than allocated whole: SGD 2.00 is returned to the rider and SGD 2.00 stands. No driver compensation is payable.\n\nFor completeness: POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider, because the driver replied 18 s after her 12:31:02 message, inside the 120 s window. POL-NS-03 does not apply, since the fixes lie inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius and registered_pickup_points is 1. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, both disputes_with_counterparty_90d counters are 0, the anti-farming check does not trip (2 no-show terminations against 146 completed trips, 1.4%), and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1. No referral is produced: the arrival marker was genuine, so POL-NS-05(ii) does not fire, and no other clause directs a review."
  },
