    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee stands as charged, and the driver is paid SGD 3.20. Under POL-GEN-03 the ruling value that names this outcome is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, and amount_sgd mirrors the compensation figure; the rider's own charge is left in place.\n\nArrival. The driver-pressed marker at 12:29:55 is not a false arrival under POL-NS-05: at that time the trace places the vehicle 18.1 m to 29.3 m from the pin, stationary, so it was neither more than 300 m away nor moving at 15 km/h or more, and the waiting clock is not recomputed on that ground. That satisfies POL-NS-01 limb (a), and the proximity test in POL-NS-02 for the STANDARD radius of 50 m (fee_schedule.arrival_radius_m, zone class STANDARD from trip_record) is met by fixes at 6.1 m to 11.9 m accuracy, well inside the 25 m filter. Limb (d) is met: the trip record shows no boarding event, started_at and ended_at are null, and the trip was terminated by the driver at 12:38:20 under cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW.\n\nThe dispute is limb (c), the dwell. The free waiting period in force is 300 seconds (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec), and POL-NS-01(c) measures it from the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 12:30:00, not from the 12:29:55 tap; the derived dwell_start_offset_sec of -5 s shows the tap and the first fix are five seconds apart, so nothing turns on the choice of clock here.\n\nEV-GPS-00211 is IMPAIRED. It carries weight 0.39 with issue codes GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW and LOW_COVERAGE: a 168-second outage from 12:33:40 to 12:36:28 falls inside the waiting window, longer than the 120-second limb of POL-NS-08(b), and coverage is 84.3 per cent. I reject the rider's reading that the effective dwell is only the 220-second first run and that the fee is therefore refundable under POL-NS-06. An impaired stretch is undecided, not a departure: this trace records no fix placing the driver outside the arrival radius at any point, the excursion entry for the