    "explanation": "To both parties. The $4.00 no-show cancellation fee on trip TRP-00211 stands as charged, and the driver is paid $3.20 of it (80 per cent, the platform retaining the remaining $0.80). This is a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling, so amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd carry the same figure.\n\nWhy the fee stands. The trip was accepted at 12:20:30. The driver marked 'arrived' at 12:29:55 and cancelled at 12:38:20 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW — about eight and a half minutes, against the 300-second (5-minute) free waiting period this trip's platform policy sets. His GPS places him 18.1 m to 29.3 m from the pickup pin at 6.1 m to 11.9 m reported accuracy, so he was inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius and stationary; his marker was therefore not a false arrival under POL-NS-05 (nowhere near the 300 m or 15 km/h threshold). The record shows no boarding and no trip start, and RIDER_NO_SHOW is a reason code the clause recognises. The fare line equals the fee in force, so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged. On those facts all four conditions of the baseline no-show test (POL-NS-01) are met and POL-NS-07 fixes the payout.\n\nThe rider's objection, and why it fails. The rider's central claim was that the longest continuous run the trace records inside the pickup fence is 220 seconds (12:30:00 to 12:33:40) — 80 seconds short of the 300-second minimum — so that POL-NS-06 makes the fee unchargeable. That reading treats a recording gap as a departure, which is wrong. EV-GPS-00211 has a 168-second gap from 12:33:40 to 12:36:28, inside the waiting window; a gap longer than 120 seconds inside the window is a policy-level impairment under POL-NS-08(b), and the trace carries weight 0.39 on issue codes GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW and LOW_COVERAGE (coverage 84.3 per cent). The trace holds no fix placing the driver outside the radius, and the 'excursion' it reports has no fixes and no measured distance — so the trace alone establishes neither that he stayed nor that he left. It therefore cannot alone prove the shortfall the rider needs; POL-NS-08(b) makes it a down-weighted carrier, not a finding of absence.\n\nThe gap is bridged, so the shortfall claim fails. The chat log EV-CHAT-00211 is complete at weight 1.0 and is not a restatement of the GPS: at 12:35:10, inside the unobserved stretch and between two admitted in-fence readings, the driver wrote 'boss still here waiting ah, cannot see you'. A contemporaneous message written from inside the stretch the trace could not observe is independent evidence of what he was doing then (the admissibility report itself calls it the only unimpaired evidence bearing on that interval), and it would still support the finding if the trace were removed. It therefore carries the deciding fact alongside the trace, so the trace is not the only evidence for the driver's presence and the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is the maximum of the two weights — 1.0, not 0.39. On that basis the driver's in-fence presence runs from the first qualifying fix at 12:30:00 to the cancellation at 12:38:20, 500 seconds, which meets the 300-second minimum. The summing route in POL-NS-06(i) is not needed and is not used: the finding is a single continuous presence, and the missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00211-01 (weight 0.0) affects only that unavailable route, so nothing is asserted against the absent artifact.\n\nThe rider's other route fails on its own terms. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate her: the driver replied 18 seconds after her 12:31:02 message, well inside the clause's 120-second window, so limb (b) fails and the clause cannot apply whatever the reply said. Her full 4.00 refund claim therefore fails.\n\nThe driver's own claims. I accept limb (a) (arrival event), limb (b) (inside the 50 m radius at the marker), the POL-NS-05 finding (marker not false), limb (d) (no boarding, driver-terminated under RIDER_NO_SHOW after the dwell), the chat-log bridging argument, and the POL-NS-07 computation. I do not accept the driver's alternative that trip_record.wait_time_min of 8.4 minutes is an independent carrier: this trip's arrival marker is a driver-pressed BUTTON, so POL-NS-12 does not apply, and that figure runs from the arrival tap rather than from the first qualifying in-fence fix, so it is not an independent measurement of the POL-NS-01(c) dwell. The chat log, not the trip record, is the independent carrier. POL-NS-03 has no application — the driver's stationary fixes are inside the arrival radius, not outside it — and POL-NS-01's in-radius FULL_REFUND outcome is confined by that clause's own notes to a DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE reason code, which this trip does not carry.\n\nEscalation, referrals and profiles. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: neither disputes_with_counterparty_90d counter reaches 2, the rider's no_show_disputes_30d is 1 (not 3 or more), the anti-farming check on driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d (2) and completed_trips_30d (146) gives 1.4 per cent, below both the count of 4 and the rate of 8 per cent, and the deciding fact is not carried by impaired evidence alone. The rider's mention of prior_no_show_flags is a context-only field under POL-GEN-01 and was not used as a ground. No clause on these facts produces a referral, so referrals is empty.\n\nConfidence. The deciding fact is carried by EV-CHAT-00211 (weight 1.0) and EV-GPS-00211 (weight 0.39), independent of each other, so the cap is the maximum, 1.0. I set confidence at 0.85, above the 0.70 escalation floor, allowing for the part of the gap the chat log does not itself observe. The monetary effect is $3.20, below the $8.00 automatic-execution threshold."
  },
